      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the number of different settings for the suitcase lock with 3 distinct digits where each digit ranges from 0 to 9, we can proceed as follows:\n\n1. **Choosing the first digit:**\n   - Any digit from 0 to 9 can be used for the first position.\n   - Therefore, there are 10 possibilities for the first digit.\n\n2. **Choosing the second digit:**\n   - The second digit cannot be the same as the first digit.\n   - Therefore, we have 9 possible choices for the second digit (noting that 0 gives more possibilities compared to the first digit).\n\n3. **Choosing the third digit:**\n   - The third digit cannot be the same as either of the first two digits.\n   - Therefore, there are 8 possible choices for the third digit (ensuring it is distinct from both the first and second digits).\n\nWe multiply these choices together to get the total number of distinct digit combinations:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 9 \\times 8\n\\]\n\nCalculating each step, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 9 = 90\n\\]\n\\[\n90 \\times 8 = 720\n\\]\n\nSo, the total number of different settings possible for the lock is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{720}\n\\]",
